  m_FontData:
    m_Font: {fileID: 10102, guid: 0000000000000000e000000000000000, type: 0}
    m_FontSize: 20
    m_FontStyle: 0
    m_BestFit: 0
    m_MinSize: 0
    m_MaxSize: 40
    m_Alignment: 0
    m_AlignByGeometry: 0
    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: "<B>Scenario</B>\nAn elderly person or someone with limited mobility often
    forgets to switch off\r\nthe room lights during the day and finds it difficult
    to locate or reach the switch in the\r\ndark at night.\r\n\n<B>Problem Statement</B>\n
    Design an Arduino-based system that automatically turns lights\r\nON during the
    night and OFF during the day using a light-dependent sensor.\r\n\n<B>Components:</B>\r\n\u2022
    Arduino Uno\r\n\u2022 LDR (Light Dependent Resistor) Sensor\r\n\u2022 LED or
    Bulb (as Load)\r\n\u2022 Jumper Wires, resistor, and Breadboard\r\n\n<B>How It
    Works:\r</B>\nThe LDR sensor continuously monitors the ambient light level for
    a set threshold. For its\r\nlower values (indicating night), the Arduino switches
    ON the light. Whereas, for its\r\nhigher values (during the day), the Arduino
    turns the light OFF to conserve energy. This\r\nautomatic operation ensures comfort
    and safety, particularly for elderly individuals or\r\nthose with limited mobility
    who may find it difficult to operate switches manually."
